{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794305773784,"sessionID":"ses_e3b0efd89ffeAYD3w6ttov37XP","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_84c5d70755c945bfa04a4062","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 -m venv /tmp/venv && /tmp/venv/bin/pip install -q -r /workspace/backend/requirements.txt -c /workspace/backend/requirements.lock 2>&1 | tail -2; /tmp/venv/bin/python -c \"import flask, gunicorn; print('backend deps ok')\"","timeout":180000},"output":"ERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements. Here is a list of those requirements along with the hashes their downloaded archives actually had. Add lines like these to your requirements files to prevent tampering. (If you did not enable --require-hashes manually, note that it turns on automatically when any package has a hash.)\n    flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, gunicorn; print('backend deps ok')\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\n","metadata":{"output":"ERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements. Here is a list of those requirements along with the hashes their downloaded archives actually had. Add lines like these to your requirements files to prevent tampering. (If you did not enable --require-hashes manually, note that it turns on automatically when any package has a hash.)\n    flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, gunicorn; print('backend deps ok')\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 -m venv /tmp/venv && /tmp/venv/bin/pip install -q -r /workspace/backend/require